# logs: the default arrangement, plus a second window to tail things in.
#
#   [main]                          [logs]
#   +-------------+-------------+   +---------------------------+
#   |  yours      |  the agent  |   |                           |
#   +-------------+-------------+   |  a full-window shell      |
#   |  scratch (5-10 lines)     |   |                           |
#   +---------------------------+   +---------------------------+
#
# For a project where something long-running wants its own window rather than
# the few lines the scratch pane gives it: a build watcher, journalctl -f, a
# dev server. The session still OPENS on the agent in [main]; prefix-n tabs to
# [logs].
#
# The window opens on a plain shell rather than a command, because what you
# want tailed is per-project. To pin one, copy this to $MUX_DIR/layouts and put
# a command on the pane, e.g. `pane journalctl -fu myservice`.
window  main
pane
pane    agent
bottom  5-10
window  logs
pane
